      "text": "```\nMATERIAL          WHEN FURNITURE-VIABLE  ENABLED BY               KEY FURNITURE APPLICATION\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nTubular steel     1920s                  Bicycle/pipe industry     Bauhaus cantilever chairs\nBent/molded ply   1930s–45              Aircraft/Navy production  Aalto L-leg, Eames DCM\nFiberglass (GRP)  Late 1940s            Boat hull production      Eames shell chair\nPolyurethane foam 1950s–60s            Chemical industry         Replaces springs + hair\nDie-cast aluminum 1950s                Aircraft production        Eames 670 base\nInjection-molded  1960s–70s            Consumer goods            Panton Chair, Kartell\npolypropylene\nCNC-cut MDF/ply   1980s                Manufacturing automation   Flat-pack precision\nCNC-cut solid wood 1990s–2000s        Manufacturing automation   Custom furniture at scale\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n```"
